<section class="sec" style="background:var(--panel);border-top:1px solid var(--border);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)">
<div class="wrap">
<h2>Why an AI Render Can't Be Printed As-Is</h2>
<p class="lead">This is the part people underestimate &mdash; and the reason most "AI jersey generator" websites stop at pretty pictures. An image is not a garment.</p>
<div class="grid3">
<div class="card"><span class="n">01</span><h3>Seams &amp; panels</h3><p>AI draws one flat torso. A real jersey is cut from front, back, sleeve and collar panels &mdash; the pattern has to wrap and align across every seam, or it looks broken on the field.</p></div>
<div class="card"><span class="n">02</span><h3>Vectorization</h3><p>Renders are low-resolution pixels. Print needs clean vector shapes at fabric scale. Our designers redraw crests, graphics and lettering so they stay sharp at every size.</p></div>
<div class="card"><span class="n">03</span><h3>Color for fabric</h3><p>Screen RGB and sublimated polyester are different worlds. We color-manage every design for dye-sublimation so the jersey you receive matches the concept you fell in love with.</p></div>
<div class="card"><span class="n">04</span><h3>The details AI forgets</h3><p>Number placement, name arcs, sponsor zones, collar construction, size grading. A concept becomes a jersey when someone who makes jerseys for a living resolves all of it.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec">
<div class="wrap">
<h2>Who Sends Us Concepts</h2>
<p class="lead">Mostly teams. Increasingly &mdash; everyone else.</p>
<div class="grid3">
<div class="card"><h3>Clubs &amp; teams</h3><p>From rec league to youth academies: a coach or player prompts a concept, the group argues about it for two weeks, and we make the winning version real. Full uniforms, numbers, names and sponsors.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Hobbyists &amp; designers</h3><p>Concept-jersey creators who want their work off the screen. A design student recently had her portfolio concept manufactured as a one-off &mdash; a real garment beats a render in any portfolio.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Gifts &amp; occasions</h3><p>A surprise jersey with a name and number on it is a gift nobody forgets. Birthdays, a teammate's last game, and bachelor party jerseys the whole group keeps.</p></div>
</div>
